# Frontend build-time configuration.
# Copy to `.env.local` for local builds, or set these as Vercel Project
# Environment Variables (they are inlined at BUILD time, not read at runtime).
#
# The API host is separate from this app: Vercel serves the static bundle,
# while the Flask API + WebSockets run on a host that keeps long-lived
# connections (Vercel functions cannot hold a WebSocket open).

# Absolute origin of the Flask API, without a trailing slash.
# Leave unset when the API is served on the same origin behind a reverse proxy.
# VITE_API_BASE=https://api.example.com

# Base URL used to build the WebSocket endpoints (bus telemetry :8765 and
# camera frames :8766). http/https are upgraded to ws/wss automatically.
# Leave unset to derive the sockets from the page origin.
# VITE_WS_URL=https://api.example.com
